# Source-derived semantics

- Both 120px by 120px containers use an 80px by 100px background positioning area formed by a 60px by 80px content box plus 10px padding.
- The tested `background: no-repeat url(...)` values use SVG images with no intrinsic width, height, or ratio; CSS requires the image to fill the background positioning area.
- Source order plus the red/green absolute controls makes any wrong background image size expose red; the assertion is two green boxes and no red.

# Compatibility adjustments

- Source `div { position: relative; }` is scoped to `.cover`, `.limit`, and `.test`, so the generated `.body` wrapper is not accidentally positioned. The source's inset-only absolute control is normalized to its Web used 80px by 100px geometry at `top: 10px; left: 10px`, avoiding Lynx-specific inset resolution in the image-size oracle.
- Web content-box sizing is explicit. The body keeps only the browser's horizontal 8px inset; the paragraph keeps its 1em vertical spacing, while each box keeps horizontal/bottom 8px margins to reproduce collapsed Web gaps without double-counting them in Lynx.
- Setup-only green/red backgrounds use `background-color`; the tested image shorthand remains unchanged.
- Visible instruction text uses `<text>`, and the two card-local SVG files are byte-identical to the pinned source assets.

# Current Lynx API-doc basis

- Lynx documents the surrounding background/layout primitives but does not explicitly guarantee SVG CSS-background decoding or this no-intrinsic-size fallback. Validation must remain fail-closed and follows the explicit-size SVG pilot.
